## 4. Part 3 — EntryPoint and New-Chat Handoff

Integrate the existing EntryPoint with the existing ACRL workflow.

### Requirements

- EntryPoint must identify the current canonical authority and exact source owners.
- EntryPoint must direct the new session to the existing startup integration.
- Previous progress must be reconstructed from verified source and evidence.
- Current task must always come from live `state.json`.
- Completed and pending work must be separated.
- Stale history, manifests and handoff packets must never override canonical state.
- T07 must validate restart payload integrity and checkpoint coherence.
- T30 must be reused for the existing completion/handoff boundary.

### Handoff output

The verified handoff must include:

- Project and repository identity.
- Current branch and HEAD.
- Canonical state blob SHA.
- Current gate, task and subtask.
- Completed work and acceptance evidence.
- Pending work and permitted next action.
- Changed paths and relevant source SHAs.
- Test and Actions evidence.
- Stale or unresolved findings.
- T14 resume decision.
- T07 restart-payload fingerprint.
- T30 handoff result where applicable.

The system may generate a copy-ready handoff artifact. It must not claim that a future ChatGPT session automatically consumes the artifact unless an actual supported session-ingress mechanism is independently verified.

